# Study data directories are allow-listed, not deny-listed.
#
# Only the five files below ship. Everything else that lands in a study's
# data/ is local scratch, and several of those working files carry Lenz's own
# verdict labels (lenz_verdict / lenz_score / lenz_reason). This repo must
# never publish a verdict label: the claims are sourced from Lenz, so shipping
# Lenz's answer alongside them would hand any reader a gold key the models
# were deliberately denied, and would contradict both the README and the
# paper's ethics statement. A deny-list would leak the next scratch file
# someone forgets to add; an allow-list fails closed.
#
# When adding a new study, replicate this block for its data/ directory.
studies/llm-disagreement/data/*
!studies/llm-disagreement/data/claims.json
!studies/llm-disagreement/data/results.json
!studies/llm-disagreement/data/results.jsonl
!studies/llm-disagreement/data/results.csv
!studies/llm-disagreement/data/LICENSE
